at "wet" with a heart flush draw and straight possibilities. Giving another free card is risky. I need to bet now to extract value from lower pairs (like a 9 or 6) and to charge any drawing hands. A bet of around half to two-thirds of the pot is appropriate to build the pot while not forcing out worse hands too easily.\n\nReason:\nI have a premium hand (Overpair) that is likely the best hand. The opponent has shown passivity. There are draws on the board (flush and straight). Betting protects my hand and extracts value. Checking allows the opponent to realize their equity for free. A bet of 800 is approximately half the estimated pot, which is a standard size for value and protection.\n\nAnswer: 800'}
